From: deepseek-v4-cmp170hx
Subject: [PATCH 0020] scheduler: catch degenerate repetition loops and
 hallucinated-tag "soup" mid-generation, trim, and finish cleanly
 (squashed port of ChinaBoy0618/deepseek-v4-cmp170hx's 0014/0015/0017/
 0017v2/0019/0019v2, six commits on the shared fork lineage, PLUS a new
 fuzzy varied-wording detector merged in below)

WHAT THIS FIXES. Three related degenerate-generation classes observed in
production on both this fork and ChinaBoy0618's independent deployment:

1. HALLUCINATED CONTROL-TAG "SOUP". After grammar salvage (`0019`)
   abandons structured-output enforcement, or independently at long
   context with zero grammar involvement, the checkpoint can degrade
   into emitting invented pseudo-tags that exist in neither DSML nor any
   real protocol: `<tool_calls`, `<reference`, `<empty-tool-call`,
   `</assistant>`, `<system-reminder>`, `<assistant_unitsummary>`, and
   more (full list in `_DSV4_SIG_STRINGS` below) -- observed live on
   THIS repo's own served image as an invented `<system-remember>` tag
   and a hallucinated `<tool_use><tool_name>bash</tool_name>` dialect
   neither DSML-shaped nor any known protocol. A streak (same signature
   held for `DSV4_SOUP_STREAK`, default 12, consecutive scheduler
   iterations) or cumulative-total (`DSV4_SOUP_TOTAL`, default 18, across
   the whole request -- sparse leakage that never saturates a streak)
   trips the tripwire, trims the offending tail, and finishes the
   request cleanly instead of letting it run to `max_tokens` of garbage.
   A post-salvage token budget (`DSV4_SALVAGE_TOKEN_BUDGET`, default 64)
   additionally bounds how long an unconstrained tail can run at all.

2. EXACT-REPEAT PHRASE-LOCK. Verbatim short-line stutter -- "Grep."
   repeated 326 times, "Lets reload." repeated 60+ times in one message
   -- the model announcing an action in prose without ever emitting the
   real tool call. Reported: 752/2717 assistant messages (28%) with zero
   real tool_use blocks in one production session, worsening toward the
   end. A line repeated >=5x in the trailing decode window (with a
   char-length prefilter and a separator whitelist so `---`/`===`
   dividers never trip it) triggers the same trim-and-finish path.

3. VARIED-WORDING PHRASE-LOCK (this repo's own addition, not upstream in
   ChinaBoy0618's fork). Observed live on THIS repo's served image at
   ~544k accumulated tokens: a dozen near-duplicate but never verbatim
   lines -- "Let me find the repro. / Let me check the repro. / Let me
   search for prior repro artifacts." -- sharing an opener ("let me")
   and a topic word ("repro") but literally never repeating the exact
   same line, so (2)'s exact-match check never fires on it. Merged in
   here as `_dsv4_fuzzy_rep_lines()`, a bucket-by-opener-then-require-
   shared-content-word check operating on the SAME decoded window and
   reusing the SAME streak/trim/finish machinery as (2) -- tried as a
   fallback only when the exact check finds nothing. The content-word
   requirement is what keeps a legitimate parallel-structure list ("The
   function parses...", "The function validates...", ...  -- shares an
   opener, no repeated topic) from tripping it; verified against the
   real captured loop text (fires) and three false-positive stress
   cases (does not fire): the parallel-structure list, a 14-line
   realistic agentic response using "let me" 3 times legitimately, and
   an 8-line short benign response.

PORT NOTES. Squashes ChinaBoy0618/deepseek-v4-cmp170hx's `0014`
(salvage-guard), `0015` (soup-tripwire base), `0017` (soup-signatures-
extended), `0017v2` (soup-cumulative-total), `0019` (line-repetition-
tripwire), and `0019v2` (rep-window floor) -- sequential, same file,
same reasons this repo's own `0019` port squashes five upstream commits.
Applied in a different order than their numbering (`0019`/`0019v2`
before `0017v2`, since `0017v2`'s own diff was captured against a repo
state that already included `0019`'s comments -- their numbering tracks
roughly-chronological production hotfixes, not a strictly bisectable
patch sequence) -- what ships here is the verified FINAL state as one
clean diff, not a replay of that path. `0017v2`'s hunks 2-3 were already
satisfied by content `0019`/`0019v2` introduced at the same call site;
applied only its one new line (the `_dsv4_soup_total` declaration).

Then merges this repo's own `_dsv4_fuzzy_rep_lines()` in as a sibling to
`_dsv4_rep_lines()`, called as a fallback from the same function so both
detectors share one streak counter and one trim/finish call site. One
bug found and fixed during merge: the fuzzy detector's content-word
extraction didn't strip trailing sentence punctuation, so "repro."
(end-of-sentence) and "repro" (mid-sentence) counted as different words,
fragmenting the count below threshold and producing a false negative on
the very case it was written for -- fixed by stripping
`.,!?;:"')]([` from each word before counting.

Touches `vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py` only, on top of `0019`'s
grammar-salvage/desync guards in the same file. Applies after `0019` in
glob order.
